The pause menu lists the pad controls.

Luanti's pause menu has a "Controls:" panel, filled only in touchscreen mode
(`src/client/game_formspec.cpp`, `showPauseMenu`). Under `OOPS_TARGET` it lists the
pad's bindings instead: Luanti's gamepad defaults (`src/defaultsettings.cpp`), which
Mineclonia's own settings do not change, in this pad's button names.

--- a/src/client/game_formspec.cpp
+++ b/src/client/game_formspec.cpp
@@ -374,6 +374,22 @@
 			" --> place single item to slot\n"
 			);
 	}
+#ifdef OOPS_TARGET
+	// The console pad: the defaults in `defaultsettings.cpp`, in the pad's own names.
+	else {
+		control_text = "Controls:\n"
+			"- left stick: walk\n"
+			"- right stick: look\n"
+			"- Cross: jump / Circle: sneak\n"
+			"- Square: sprint\n"
+			"- Triangle: inventory\n"
+			"- R2: dig / L2: place or use\n"
+			"- L1 / R1: hotbar slot\n"
+			"- D-pad: zoom / drop / fly\n"
+			"- Create: minimap\n"
+			"- Options: pause\n";
+	}
+#endif
 
 	auto simple_singleplayer_mode = m_client->m_simple_singleplayer_mode;
 
